# From luma-duo2 (none24smu, Apache-2.0): tie each touchscreen to its panel output.
# Surface Duo 2: duo2-touchd's two touchscreens, one per panel, each tied to
# its panel's display output. libinput reports WL_OUTPUT as the device's
# output name, and phoc maps the touchscreen to that output.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Surface Duo 2 Touchscreen Left", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="DSI-1"
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Surface Duo 2 Touchscreen Right", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="DSI-2"
# duo2-touchd's pen (the heat processor's pen reports): a tablet device per
# panel, on the same panel coordinates as that panel's touchscreen.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Surface Duo 2 Pen Left", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="DSI-1"
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Surface Duo 2 Pen Right", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="DSI-2"
# No LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX: the heat processor's x stretch and shift are
# corrected inside duo2-touchd (/etc/duo2/touch-calibration), before it clamps
# a contact to its panel; here (after the clamp) the panels' edges near the
# hinge could not be reached.
# The digitizer's own input devices (spi 045E:0C1D, Touchscreen, Stylus...:
# the kernel's single-point fallback and the firmware's own pen report, both
# with no panel) are not for the compositor: the pen comes from duo2-touchd.
# Opened by libinput, they kept the HID device open, so the digitizer was
# never powered down and up again between duo2-touchd instances, and opened
# during spi-hid's start they kept it powered off ("ready" never came).
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="spi 045E:0C1D*", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
